<title>SWEDEN: Swedbank says issues $100 mln perpetual debenture.</title>
<headline>Swedbank says issues $100 mln perpetual debenture.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish banking group Swedbank said on Friday it is issuing a $100 million perpetual debenture.  </p>
<p>The bank has the right to redeem $50 million after ten years and $50 million after 15 years on condition of approval from the Finance Inspectorate, Swedbank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The debenture is a private placement and is part of the restructuring of Swedbank Group's debentures, leading to longer duration and a larger share of perpetual debentures.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
